                <pb facs="0152" n="87" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg87"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/3422: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-01-11T01:00:00+02:00">January 11, 1936—1
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Important reinforcements of British mechanized military units arrived in Egypt
                    this week. I learn from reliable source that by the middle of next month British
                    troops in this country are expected to be considerably in excess of existing
                    strength. Divisional headquarters <pb facs="0153" n="88" xml:id="pg88"/> for the
                    forces stationed the western desert have been established at Alexandria under
                    the command of Major General Howard, recently arrived. Reenforcement and
                    strengthening of the principal British base in the western desert at Mersa
                    Matruh is proceeding apace.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
